<h1>Master Rolodex — All My Links — Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="muted">Last updated: October 26, 2026</p>

<h2>Who we are</h2>
<p>Master Rolodex — All My Links (Android app <code>com.usefulappz.masterrolodex</code>) is developed by Usefulappz™ (Mike Kelley). Contact: <a href="mailto:mikekelleyii.mk2@gmail.com">mikekelleyii.mk2@gmail.com</a></p>

<h2>The short version</h2>
<p>Master Rolodex stores every link family in one rolodex — affiliate links, socials, websites and pages, channels, storefronts, and app links, kept as sections — so a link lands once and lights up everywhere it is plugged in. It collects <strong>no personal data</strong>: no accounts, no analytics, no ads SDK, no tracking, and nothing is sold.</p>

<h2>How the app works</h2>
<ul>
  <li>The app reads the rolodex entries from <strong>our server</strong> — one public, read-only endpoint per link family — and displays them by family. Affiliate entries are always shown whole: link, code, and disclosure together.</li>
  <li>Tapping a link opens it in your <strong>system browser</strong>, outside this app. The destination site's own privacy policy applies there; any affiliate cookie is set by that destination site, not by this app.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What the app stores</h2>
<p>The rolodex entries live on our server (they are the developer's own link records — names, URLs, and codes, not information about you). The app stores nothing about you on your device beyond its own display state, and it sends us nothing about you.</p>

<h2>Permissions, and why</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Internet</strong> — used only to read the current rolodex entries from our server, as described above.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Ads</h2>
<p>Master Rolodex is a paid app. It contains <strong>no ads and no advertising SDK</strong>. The affiliate links it stores are labeled with their disclosure wherever they appear.</p>

<h2>Children</h2>
<p>Master Rolodex is a business tool. It is not directed at children under 13, and it collects no data from anyone. Entries belonging to kids'-brand worlds (Little Inkers, Poppy &amp; Ziggy) are flagged kid-safe in the rolodex; the flag describes the link, and the app itself remains a tool for the links' owner.</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted at this URL with a new "last updated" date.</p>

